.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_HEADER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_header \- look up a response header by name
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

const char *chttpclient_resp_header(const chttpcli_response *resp,
                                    const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns the value of the named response header, or NULL
if the response has no such header. The lookup ignores case, because
the response stores every header name in lowercase and the function
lowercases your name before it looks it up.

A server can send the same header name on several lines. For such a
name the function returns the combined value that RFC 9110 section 5.3
defines, which is every value in wire order joined with ", ".
Set-Cookie is the only exception: RFC 9110 section 5.3 and RFC 6265
section 3 forbid combining it (a cookie value can hold a comma of its
own), so for "set-cookie" you get the first occurrence.
chttpclient_resp_header_count and chttpclient_resp_header_at give you
each occurrence separately. The response's headers map holds the same
value for each name as this function returns.

The returned pointer stays valid until chttpclient_resp_free is
called.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
resp  The response to query. It can be NULL, in which case the
      function returns NULL.
name  The header name. It can be NULL, in which case the function
      returns NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the header's value string, or NULL if the header is not
there.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The map behind this function is built from the response's header block
only. A chunked body can carry trailer fields (RFC 7230 4.1.2), which
the client parses and validates, but those are not response headers.
So a trailer field of any name reads as absent here, and it can never
replace a header that the server actually sent.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_count (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_at (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_free (3)
